@local/dsh-element-context README · 安装：然后编辑 `$profile\package.json`，合并以下字段（已存在的字段里追加即可）：

```json
{
  "dependencies": {
    "@local/dsh-element-context": "link:C:/Users/you/code/dsh-element-context"
  },

</details>

两种方式完成后都需**重启 DeepSeek Harness**，并在「插件管理」页确认 `@local/dsh-element-context` 已启用。

@local/dsh-element-context README · Installation：New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force "$profile\node_modules\@local" | Out-Null

Then merge these fields into `$profile\package.json` (append inside existing fields):

```json
{
  "dependencies": {
    "@local/dsh-element-context": "link:C:/Users/you/code/dsh-element-context"
  },

</details>

Either way, **restart DeepSeek Harness** afterwards and confirm `@local/dsh-element-context` is enabled on the plugin management page.

@local/dsh-element-context README · Uninstall：- `host.js` (Node side): serves the `/element-context` route (guarded by the DSH connection-layer trust policy) and renders the element list from `~/.dsh/element-context.json` into the systemPrompt.
- `client.js` (browser side): the composer dock (manual input + chips) and the pick probe. The desktop browser is an Electron `<webview>`; the client acts as the embedder, injects the probe with `executeJavaScript`, and reads captures back by polling.

</details>
